<font size="3" face="helvetica,arial" color="FF0300"><b>Not Just One, But TWO PLANES In One Day!</b></font>
<p>
<font size="2" face="helvetica,arial" color="FE9700"><b>One year ago, if you asked me if we would ever get an epic in SoD, I would have said I was uncertain. Six months ago, if you asked me the same question, I would have said "maybe" we would obtain the shaman epic one day, being one of the easier ones, and one I was most familiar with. 
<p>
Three months ago, we got our first Shaman epic, with the help of Eternal Heroes and a few close friends, congratulations to Bobmd being the first player in SoD with their epic weapon. 
<p>
One month ago, Serj was the second Shaman in SoD to acquire their epic spear. Congratulations to Serj. Two weeks ago, we helped Alailya finish her Druid Epic. Congratulations to Alailya on a long quest well done! 
<p>
<a href="images/xetus_epic/serj_epic.jpg"><img border="2" align="right" width="200" height="150" vspace="10" hspace="5" src="images/xetus_epic/serj_epic.gif"></a>So today, if you ask me, "Hey Bob, can we do my epic mob in Fear? Can we do my epic mob in Hate? Can we take down Faydedar?" I will reply, "What day is good for you?" 
<p>
I cannot tell you how impressed and proud I am of how much we've grown as a team, and as a guild. I get tells every day asking if people can join our team, and how they've heard so much about how we've grown, and that basically, it's fun to be part of an organization that is in it's upswing, moving on to bigger and better things, exploring new territories together for the first time etc.
<p>
I'll be the first to tell you, I'm having a blast!
<p>
<a href="images/xetus_epic/fear_golem10.jpg"><img border="2" align="left" width="200" height="150" vspace="10" hspace="5" src="images/xetus_epic/fear_golem10.gif"></a>After weeks of negotiation and research, we studied the Wizard epic in close detail and narrowed down a few big battles that must be won before a wizard epic can be wielded by a SoD wizard. 
<p>
A level 63 golem in the plane of Fear is one, and the plane must be cleared first, before a safe attempt at the golem can be considered. The troops gathered for this man, Xetus Cringefist!
<p>
After playing "Gnome-Ball"&#153; with him for a few hours, we got down to business...
<p>
<a href="images/xetus_epic/fear_portal.jpg"><img border="2" align="right" width="200" height="150" vspace="10" hspace="5" src="images/xetus_epic/fear_portal.gif"></a>Five groups of our most worthy adventurers gathered at the portal to the dreaded Plane of Fear, only accessable to the most hardened of players; only the most wise and determined... err, you have to be level 46+ to get in. 
<p>
<a href="images/xetus_epic/fear_mobs1.jpg"><img border="2" align="left" width="200" height="150" vspace="10" hspace="5" src="images/xetus_epic/fear_mobs1.gif"></a>Two groups of six brave souls entered the plane, nervous and eager to see what awaited us on the other side. Lucky for us, there was no initial agro, and the camp site was safe for the rest to join the break-in crew. 
<p>
Five groups made it to the camp safely and we began to successfully clear the plane of any "fearful" inhabitants with minimal injuries to our team.
<p>
<a href="images/xetus_epic/fear_golem12.jpg"><img border="2" align="right" width="200" height="150" vspace="10" hspace="5" src="images/xetus_epic/fear_golem12.gif"></a>When all that was left was the golem, we formed a circle around the little guy and had Xetus spawn his big brother, a level 63, non-casting brute, with about 300,000 hit points and AC up the ying-yang, which hit in the 400's. 
<p>
With the help of Tunor (level 60 ranger) who tanked the golem like a champ, and Artian (level 60 cleric) who has unlimited mana (it seems), we were able to take down the golem.  
<p>
<a href="images/xetus_epic/fear_golem14.jpg"><img border="2" align="left" width="200" height="150" vspace="10" hspace="5" src="images/xetus_epic/fear_golem14.gif"></a>With a fight that seemed to take 15 minutes, we slowly worked his hit points down to a managable level, ultimately slaying the beast. 
<p>
Congratulations to Xetus on furthering his epic quest and who one day, will no doubt, wield the Wizard Epic.
<p>
<a href="images/xetus_epic/fear_golem16.jpg"><img border="2" align="right" width="200" height="150" vspace="10" hspace="5" src="images/xetus_epic/fear_golem16.gif"></a>We stood and celebrated as Xetus looted his epic piece and there was much rejoicing. 
<p>
Artian and Tunor were given SoD's youngest virgins as payment for their noble deeds, and we thank them heartily for their assistance. But that wasn't all...
<p>
Earlier that day, being the adventurous type that we are, we decided to throw together a pick-up raid to the Plane of Hate, to acquire some much needed Chanter and Pally epic pieces. An early wipeout didn't stop the determined forces, only brought help from deep within SoD to overcome the "hateful" mobs that lurk near the portal. 
<p>
<a href="images/xetus_epic/Hex51.jpg"><img border="2" align="left" width="200" height="150" vspace="10" hspace="5" src="images/xetus_epic/Hex51.gif"></a>With excellent work by Annoly and Jamethiel, the mobs were kept at bay while the SoD "swat team" took down any offenders who got in our way. 
<p>
The new clothes were dropping like a "sale at Macy's" and many of the adventurers went home with shiny new armor, including a Warrior Breastplate, Bard Vambs, Cleric Bracer and Boots, Mage Gloves and a few other nice pieces. Congratulations to everyone for an excellent raid.
<p>
<a href="images/xetus_epic/vt.jpg"><img border="2" align="right" width="200" height="150" vspace="10" hspace="5" src="images/xetus_epic/vt.gif"></a>Maybe some day soon, we will find ourselves inside a murky place not unlike the dreary, much-unknown, cavernous, dragon-filled dungeon, ruled by Veeshan, located in the heart of the deadly Skyfire Mountains, called Veeshan's Peak. There are nothing but Veeshan-worshiping, deadly dragons located inside, but we will find out ourselves, so stay tuned for more... "As SoD Turns".
<p>
<a href="images/xetus_epic/vespina_stuck.jpg"><img border="2" align="left" width="200" height="150" vspace="10" hspace="5" src="images/xetus_epic/vespina_stuck.gif"></a> Unfortunately, Vespina could not make it to the raid, as she was stuck in a rock in Velketor's Lab ;p
<p>

</b></font>





<p><font face="helvetica,arial" size="4" color="000000"><b>-</b></font></p>
<p align="justify"><font face="helvetica,arial" size="2" color="000000"><b></b></font></p>

